{"turn_id":"85671d10-b7db-4811-b0d8-a5011c98ea35","thread_id":"c1d2f74f-95b9-4aba-a105-126d2a65d6ac","sequence":15,"role":"assistant","content":"Agreed: the collective displacement emerged during loading and unloading, rather than being an independently imposed rigid shift. I retained that motion—**no rigid alignment or displacement subtraction was applied**.\n\nThe **18-replica NEB calculation completed** between the initial and unloaded **zero-strain configurations**, retaining the shear-boundary constraints and continuous periodic x geometry.\n\n## Minimum Energy Path\n\n![NEB energy path between zero-strain configurations](artifacts/analysis/neb/neb-analysis-20261021-215038-5ed9de/neb_mep.png)\n\nThe sampled profile contains **one saddle candidate and no intermediate local minima**: energy rises to the saddle and then falls toward the unloaded configuration.\n\n| Quantity | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| Saddle reaction coordinate | **0.5781** |\n| Forward barrier: initial → unloaded | **0.08515 eV** |\n| Reverse barrier: unloaded → initial | **0.10108 eV** |\n| Unloaded minus initial energy | **−0.01594 eV** |\n\nThese energies refer to the **entire simulated cell**, not individual atoms.\n\n### Interpretation\n\nThe calculated path is consistent with **two distinct configurations connected by an energy barrier**, with the unloaded state slightly lower in energy. It therefore provides a plausible energetic transition between the states observed before and after loading.\n\nHowever:\n\n- **NEB force convergence remains unverified** from the available output, so these are **sampled-profile barrier estimates**, not yet validated activation energies.\n- The finite replica spacing and sharp decrease after the saddle limit its precise localization.\n- This constrained path does **not reconstruct the actual shear-driven trajectory** or establish a unique atomic mechanism.\n\nThe most informative next inspection would be the **replica structures before, at, and after the saddle**, to identify which collective motions and local GB rearrangements produce the energy change.\n\n**NEB run:** `neb-20261021-214036-574393`  \n[Raw MEP CSV](artifacts/lammps/neb/neb-20261021-214036-574393/mep_profile.csv) · [Saddle/barrier analysis](artifacts/analysis/neb/neb-analysis-20261021-215038-ae08e5/neb_mep_analysis.json)","reasoning":"","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:39:51+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-21T21:51:11+00:00","image_paths":["artifacts/analysis/neb/neb-analysis-20261021-215038-5ed9de/neb_mep.png"],"trace":[{"event_id":"7093e8fb-c29e-47cb-a4b4-0a73603ee5f6","turn_id":"85671d10-b7db-4811-b0d8-a5011c98ea35","parent_event_id":null,"tool_call_id":null,"sequence":0,"event_type":"reasoning_withheld","tool_name":null,"label":null,"input_json":"{\"reasoning_tokens\": 56}","output_text":"","status":"completed","started_at":null,"completed_at":"2026-10-21T21:40:06+00:00","image_paths":[]},{"event_id":"18aa08f5-e792-4a9a-a8c3-318284f7c600","turn_id":"85671d10-b7db-4811-b0d8-a5011c98ea35","parent_event_id":null,"tool_call_id":"call_eKk4eEkMSvXEippgX2FpMjbt","sequence":1,"event_type":"tool_start","tool_name":"delegate_lammps","label":"LAMMPS agent","input_json":"User explicitly requests NEB and MEP to investigate intermediate transition between initial and unloaded ZERO cumulative strain configurations after prior x loading/unloading, not reload final. Execute NEB for exact endpoints: INITIAL shear-20261021-203147-9d18c4 role intermediate_structure step0 artifact ed6fdc81-7786-59b4-9671-fb6729be1245; FINAL shear-20261021-211934-d84742 role intermediate_structure localstep70 artifact f640db04-3a6e-5cba-acdc-df7d9a1bdfde. Both selected shear frames converged,11052 matched IDs, cumulative strain0. Use source shear input/config to preserve NiCr.adp adp FCC Ni a0=3.52A,continuous periodic x existing box/grain order. Retain actual shear top/bottom boundary-ID constraints constraint_mode=shear_boundaries (both zero strain same prescribed boundar